1
00:01:34,400 --> 00:01:36,560
After attending girls' school at high school-

2
00:01:36,720 --> 00:01:40,200
-Moves Karin to Uppsala to go to university.

3
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:44,280
A male -dominated environment where female students are unusual.

4
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:49,560
Karin gets her eyes on how unequal women are treated in teaching.

5
00:01:49,720 --> 00:01:55,240
She had been staying in girl environments, so this with inequality-

6
00:01:55,400 --> 00:02:00,480
-In how boys and girls were treated would not have been a matter for her.

7
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:04,320
Now she came to a very male -dominated environment.

8
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:06,640
One in many ways conservative environment-

9
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:11,280
-There the girls, the student shoes were something unusual.

10
00:02:28,880 --> 00:02:33,640
She gathered her best old poems and went to Bonniers publisher-

11
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:38,040
-To Karl Otto Bonnier and asked if she could be published.

12
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:43,640
After only a few weeks they heard from them and said, "Yes, you are accepted."

13
00:02:43,800 --> 00:02:49,240
So she was 21 years old.
It was something very unique then.

14
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:55,120
The debut book "Cloud" is a collection of poems about a young man's pondering.

15
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:59,000
About life, about God, about his own future.

16
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:02,880
Suddenly she became a celebrity in Uppsala, a literary celebrity-

17
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:05,640
-So then she got into these author gangs.

18
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,640
Then she became more politically radicalized too.

19
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:18,160
-and it was the next logical step to detect the injustices between class-

20
00:03:18,320 --> 00:03:21,080
-and between different countries.

21
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:26,480
Interest in politics and how people in other countries had it-

22
00:03:26,640 --> 00:03:29,840
-Growing with Karin and she started traveling.

23
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,680
Among other things, she goes to the then Soviet Union and is struck by the oppression.

24
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:40,680
1932 she travels to Berlin, the year before Hitler takes power-

25
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:44,120
-and sees how Nazism begins to permeate society-

26
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:48,360
-But then without understanding the seriousness, as for so many others.

27
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,720
She is curious and observes.
Fascination mixed with fear-

28
00:03:52,880 --> 00:03:55,640
-What is visible in her texts.

29
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:05,240
But the trip down to Germany she not only did for the sake of travel.

30
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:26,560
This life force has been lost.

31
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:31,880
It is important to come back to this living Karin Boye.

32
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:37,560
Yes, it hurts when buds are lacking.

33
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:41,800
Why else would spring hesitate?

34
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:48,800
Why would all our hot longing be tied in the frozen bitter pale?

35
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:53,760
After all, the casing was the bud all winter.

36
00:11:18,760 --> 00:11:22,760
Texting: Elin CSisar www.btistudios.com
